                    We can recognize the pattern in ordinary life. Recognition satisfies briefly, then demands a larger audience. Money solves real problems, yet no amount can abolish mortality or guarantee love. A relationship may be a profound vocation, but another human being cannot bear the role of savior. Pleasure can refresh and bond, but pursued as an absolute it often loses even its natural joy. Created goods disappoint most cruelly when we demand divinity from them.

